# Cross-boundary declarations for ussrd (NVIDIA PHS power-management daemon).
#
# The ussrd process itself runs as a vendor daemon — its `type ussrd, domain`
# and `init_daemon_domain(ussrd)` stay in sepolicy/vendor/ussrd.te. Platform
# components (system_server, surfaceflinger, mediaserver, cameraserver, etc.)
# need to reach it through service_manager and connect to /dev/socket/phsd,
# so those touch-points are declared here in public/ where both compilation
# units (plat_sepolicy and vendor_sepolicy) can see them.
#
# The `ussrd_domain` attribute is the platform-visible handle for the
# concrete `ussrd` type; vendor/ussrd.te attaches it via typeattribute.
# Putting `type ussrd` directly in public/ would auto-tag it `coredomain`
# and trip AOSP neverallow rules, since ussrd is a /vendor/bin binary.
attribute ussrd_domain;
type ussrd_service, service_manager_type;
